-- Version: 0.23.8
-- Description: Split service-request approval from work-item lifecycle status,
--   rename service-request SQL objects to the work_item_* naming convention,
--   add generic KB per-entity content_version/content_hash columns, and bring
--   catalog-visibility parity for services and work-item forms. One
--   migration: none of these had shipped in a release when they were drafted,
--   so they land in the same unreleased version instead of adjacent files.
-- Backend file: m_0.23.8_work_item_status_and_naming.sql
--
-- Changes in v0.23.8:
-- - New enum app.work_item_approval_status (not_required / pending / approved /
--   auto_approved / rejected / auto_rejected / cancelled) — approval outcome,
--   decoupled from the work item's own lifecycle status.
-- - New enum app.work_item_status (new / in_progress / paused / resolved /
--   reopened / closed / cancelled / failed), practice-neutral, replaces
--   app.request_status. Removed values (pending_approval / approved /
--   rejected) move to work_item_approval_status; failed is kept as a general
--   "execution did not complete" terminal status.
-- - app.service_requests renamed to app.work_item_service_requests.
--   approval_status added as its last column (NOT NULL DEFAULT not_required),
--   backfilled from the pre-change status value. status retyped from
--   app.request_status to app.work_item_status with old values remapped
--   (pending_approval/approved -> in_progress, rejected -> closed).
--   app.request_status dropped.
-- - Five shared enums renamed to the work_item_ convention, values unchanged:
--   request_urgency -> work_item_urgency, request_impact -> work_item_impact,
--   request_priority -> work_item_priority, request_pause_reason ->
--   work_item_pause_reason, request_channel -> work_item_channel.
-- - Sequence, indexes, triggers, trigger functions and named/implicit
--   PK/FK/CHECK/UNIQUE constraints on the table follow the new table name.
-- - Leftover service_requests_*_not_null constraints are renamed to
--   work_item_service_requests_*_not_null so rehearsal pg_dump matches a
--   fresh install (PG 16+ stores NOT NULL as named catalog objects;
--   RENAME TABLE does not rewrite those names).
-- - Added app.kb_trees.content_version/content_hash, app.kb_nodes.content_version/content_hash, app.kb_articles.content_version/content_hash — generic per-entity content revision stamp (BIGINT counter + sha256 hash), independent of system_content_version/hash. Non-destructive, additive only.
-- - Synced the built-in HELP KB tree content from db/kb-system/users.sql (v1.17.0): every kb_trees/kb_nodes/kb_articles row now carries its content_version=1 and content_hash. No documentation text changed — infrastructure only.
-- - Moved the two landing settings from Application.Appearance to
--   Application.System.Modules; existing value preserved.
-- - Application.Appearance theme.mode factory default is now system; existing
--   value is preserved.
-- - New enums app.service_operational_status (available /
--   planned_maintenance / emergency_maintenance / paused) and
--   app.service_pause_reason (business / security / other).
-- - app.services gains operational_status, pause_reason, catalog_visible
--   (last columns). Backfill from the old status column, then drop status,
--   service_type and priority. Drop types app.service_status,
--   app.service_type, app.service_priority. CHECK chk_services_pause_reason
--   ties pause_reason to operational_status = paused.
-- - app.section_services: drop uq_section_services_service; add "order"
--   (INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0) as last column. A service may be in N
--   sections; "order" is the grid position.
-- - Drop app.work_item_forms.status and chk_work_item_forms_active_has_version;
--   drop type app.work_item_form_status. catalog_visible default becomes
--   false. Rename work_item_form_version_status value published → active.
--   current_version_id must point at an active version.
-- - Replace idx_work_item_forms_kind_status and
--   idx_work_item_forms_service_status_order with indexes that do not use
--   form identity status.
-- - COMMENT ON work_item_forms.catalog_order (1-based when bound; 0 when unbound)
--   and idempotent per-service 1..N backfill of bound catalog_order values.
--
-- Destructive-affects: COLUMN app.service_requests.status; TABLE app.service_requests; TYPE app.request_status, app.request_urgency, app.request_impact, app.request_priority, app.request_pause_reason, app.request_channel; SEQUENCE app.seq_service_request_number; app.app_settings keys (Application.Appearance, default.module.anonymous.users) and (Application.Appearance, default.module.registered.users) — section_path only; COLUMN app.services.status; COLUMN app.services.service_type; COLUMN app.services.priority; COLUMN app.work_item_forms.status; TYPE app.service_status; TYPE app.service_type; TYPE app.service_priority; TYPE app.work_item_form_status; CONSTRAINT app.section_services.uq_section_services_service; ENUM VALUE app.work_item_form_version_status.published
-- Destructive-data-loss: existing service_requests.status values pending_approval and approved become in_progress; rejected becomes closed. The original approval-related status is copied onto approval_status (pending/approved/rejected) only when that column is still not_required. app.request_status is dropped. Every other rename in this file is metadata-only (table/sequence/index/trigger/function/constraint identity changes; no rows rewritten, no other data lost). None for the two landing settings — value is preserved; old (Application.Appearance, default.module.*) keys cease to exist. app.services.status values are mapped into operational_status / pause_reason / catalog_visible then discarded (under_maintenance → planned_maintenance, suspended → paused + pause_reason other, else available; catalog_visible = status was active). app.services.service_type and app.services.priority values are discarded with no successor. app.work_item_forms.status values are discarded (draft / active / archived). Existing form catalog_visible values are kept; only the column default becomes false.
--
-- Idempotency: enum/table/sequence/index/trigger/function/constraint renames
--   are guarded by an existence check on the old name, so a second run after
--   the rename already happened is a no-op. The status backfill and column
--   retype are guarded by checking the column's current declared type.
--   CREATE OR REPLACE keeps function bodies current on re-apply. The settings
--   move is guarded (UPDATE only when the new key is absent; INSERT ON CONFLICT
--   updates product-owned columns only; leftover old keys are deleted).
--   theme.mode factory default is upserted (INSERT ON CONFLICT updates
--   product-owned columns only; existing value is never overwritten).
--   Catalog-visibility: CREATE TYPE swallows duplicate_object. ADD COLUMN /
--   CREATE INDEX use IF NOT EXISTS. ADD CONSTRAINT swallows duplicate_object.
--   DROP COLUMN / DROP TYPE / DROP INDEX / DROP CONSTRAINT use IF EXISTS.
--   Services backfill runs only while app.services.status still exists.
--   RENAME VALUE published → active runs only while that enum label is still
--   present. CREATE OR REPLACE keeps the form current-version trigger
--   function current.
--   COMMENT ON app.work_item_forms.catalog_order is re-runnable. The
--   per-service catalog_order 1..N backfill is identity once rows are
--   already 1..N (same ORDER BY catalog_order, created_at, id).
--   Re-running this file after a first successful apply is a no-op end to end.
--
-- Applies to upgrades from released 0.23.7 (schema has been unchanged since
-- 0.23.2 — 0.23.3 through 0.23.7 were version-only stamps). Fresh installs
-- take the final shape directly from db/init and skip this file entirely
-- (schema_version already 0.23.8).

BEGIN;

-- ===========================================================================
-- 1. New enums — final names from the start, no intermediate naming
-- ===========================================================================

DO $$ BEGIN
    CREATE TYPE app.work_item_status AS ENUM (
        'new', 'in_progress', 'paused', 'resolved',
        'reopened', 'closed', 'cancelled', 'failed'
    );
EXCEPTION
    WHEN duplicate_object THEN NULL;
END $$;

COMMENT ON TYPE app.work_item_status IS
    'Practice-neutral lifecycle status for a work item: new, in_progress, paused, resolved, reopened, closed, cancelled, failed. Reusable across all app.work_item_kind practices (service_request, incident, problem, change, release) even though only service_request has a table today.';

DO $$ BEGIN
    CREATE TYPE app.work_item_approval_status AS ENUM (
        'not_required', 'pending', 'approved', 'auto_approved',
        'rejected', 'auto_rejected', 'cancelled'
    );
EXCEPTION
    WHEN duplicate_object THEN NULL;
END $$;

COMMENT ON TYPE app.work_item_approval_status IS
    'Approval outcome for a work item, decoupled from the work item''s own lifecycle status (app.work_item_status). not_required is the default for most requests. auto_approved and auto_rejected record decisions made by a business rule or automation rather than a human approver, for audit clarity. No fill or compute logic exists yet — this release only defines storage.';

-- ===========================================================================
-- 2. Rename the five shared enums whose value set is unchanged
-- ===========================================================================

DO $$
DECLARE
    rec record;
BEGIN
    FOR rec IN
        SELECT * FROM (VALUES
            ('request_urgency',      'work_item_urgency'),
            ('request_impact',       'work_item_impact'),
            ('request_priority',     'work_item_priority'),
            ('request_pause_reason', 'work_item_pause_reason'),
            ('request_channel',      'work_item_channel')
        ) AS t(old_name, new_name)
    LOOP
        IF EXISTS (
            SELECT 1 FROM pg_type
            WHERE typname = rec.old_name
              AND typnamespace = 'app'::regnamespace
        ) THEN
            EXECUTE format('ALTER TYPE app.%I RENAME TO %I', rec.old_name, rec.new_name);
        END IF;
    END LOOP;
END $$;

COMMENT ON TYPE app.work_item_impact IS
    'Impact levels for a service request: low, medium, high, critical (same ladder as work_item_urgency). Stored only; no fill logic and no priority calculation from impact and urgency in this release.';
COMMENT ON TYPE app.work_item_priority IS
    'Priority levels for a service request: low, medium, high, critical. Stored only; values are set manually. This release does not compute priority from impact and urgency.';
COMMENT ON TYPE app.work_item_pause_reason IS
    'Hold-reason codes for a paused service request. awaiting_requester and awaiting_third_party are outside the support team''s control, scheduled is planned work, other keeps the clock running. Stored on work_item_service_requests.pause_reason; no fill logic and no CHECK tying the column to status in this release.';

-- ===========================================================================
-- 3. Table rename (before any dependent rename that names the table)
-- ===========================================================================

DO $$
BEGIN
    IF to_regclass('app.service_requests') IS NOT NULL THEN
        ALTER TABLE app.service_requests RENAME TO work_item_service_requests;
    END IF;
END $$;

-- ===========================================================================
-- 4. approval_status column (new, appended last) + backfill
-- ===========================================================================

ALTER TABLE app.work_item_service_requests
    ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS approval_status app.work_item_approval_status
        NOT NULL DEFAULT 'not_required'::app.work_item_approval_status;

-- Backfill from the pre-change status value. Guarded so a second run — e.g.
-- re-apply due to checksum change — does not clobber administrator/runtime state.
UPDATE app.work_item_service_requests
SET approval_status = CASE status::text
    WHEN 'pending_approval' THEN 'pending'
    WHEN 'approved'         THEN 'approved'
    WHEN 'rejected'         THEN 'rejected'
    ELSE approval_status::text
END::app.work_item_approval_status
WHERE status::text IN ('pending_approval', 'approved', 'rejected')
  AND approval_status = 'not_required'::app.work_item_approval_status;

-- ===========================================================================
-- 5. Open-queue indexes: drop before retyping status (old predicates name
--    values that do not exist on app.work_item_status)
-- ===========================================================================

DROP INDEX IF EXISTS app.idx_service_requests_group_open;
DROP INDEX IF EXISTS app.idx_service_requests_assignee_open;

-- ===========================================================================
-- 6. status: app.request_status -> app.work_item_status
-- ===========================================================================

DO $$
BEGIN
    IF EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM information_schema.columns
        WHERE table_schema = 'app'
          AND table_name = 'work_item_service_requests'
          AND column_name = 'status'
          AND udt_name = 'request_status'
    ) THEN
        ALTER TABLE app.work_item_service_requests
            ALTER COLUMN status DROP DEFAULT;
        ALTER TABLE app.work_item_service_requests
            ALTER COLUMN status TYPE app.work_item_status
            USING (CASE status::text
                WHEN 'pending_approval' THEN 'in_progress'
                WHEN 'approved'         THEN 'in_progress'
                WHEN 'rejected'         THEN 'closed'
                ELSE status::text
            END)::app.work_item_status;
    END IF;
END $$;

ALTER TABLE app.work_item_service_requests
    ALTER COLUMN status SET DEFAULT 'new'::app.work_item_status;

DROP TYPE IF EXISTS app.request_status;

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_work_item_service_requests_group_open
    ON app.work_item_service_requests USING btree (assigned_group_id, created_at DESC)
    WHERE status IN ('new', 'in_progress', 'reopened', 'paused');

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_work_item_service_requests_assignee_open
    ON app.work_item_service_requests USING btree (assigned_user_id, created_at DESC)
    WHERE status IN ('new', 'in_progress', 'reopened', 'paused');

-- ===========================================================================
-- 7. Sequence
-- ===========================================================================

DO $$
BEGIN
    IF to_regclass('app.seq_service_request_number') IS NOT NULL THEN
        ALTER SEQUENCE app.seq_service_request_number
            RENAME TO seq_work_item_service_request_number;
    END IF;
END $$;

COMMENT ON SEQUENCE app.seq_work_item_service_request_number IS
    'Counter for service request numbers (base36 suffix, sr-000001..sr-zzzzzz). MAXVALUE = 36^6-1.';

-- ===========================================================================
-- 8. Remaining indexes (group_open / assignee_open already handled in step 6)
-- ===========================================================================

DO $$
DECLARE
    rec record;
BEGIN
    FOR rec IN
        SELECT * FROM (VALUES
            ('idx_service_requests_requester_created',     'idx_work_item_service_requests_requester_created'),
            ('idx_service_requests_requested_for_created', 'idx_work_item_service_requests_requested_for_created'),
            ('idx_service_requests_service_status',        'idx_work_item_service_requests_service_status'),
            ('idx_service_requests_answers',               'idx_work_item_service_requests_answers'),
            ('idx_service_requests_title_trgm',            'idx_work_item_service_requests_title_trgm'),
            ('idx_service_requests_form_version',          'idx_work_item_service_requests_form_version')
        ) AS t(old_name, new_name)
    LOOP
        IF to_regclass('app.' || rec.old_name) IS NOT NULL THEN
            EXECUTE format('ALTER INDEX app.%I RENAME TO %I', rec.old_name, rec.new_name);
        END IF;
    END LOOP;
END $$;

-- ===========================================================================
-- 9. Constraints (named CHECKs/UNIQUE plus implicit PK/FKs from CREATE TABLE,
--    plus PG 16+ named NOT NULL constraints `{table}_{column}_not_null`,
--    which RENAME TABLE does not rewrite)
-- ===========================================================================

DO $$
DECLARE
    rec record;
BEGIN
    FOR rec IN
        SELECT * FROM (VALUES
            ('uq_service_requests_request_number',          'uq_work_item_service_requests_request_number'),
            ('chk_service_requests_request_number_format',  'chk_work_item_service_requests_request_number_format'),
            ('chk_service_requests_title_not_blank',        'chk_work_item_service_requests_title_not_blank'),
            ('chk_service_requests_answers_object',         'chk_work_item_service_requests_answers_object'),
            ('service_requests_pkey',                       'work_item_service_requests_pkey'),
            ('service_requests_service_id_fkey',            'work_item_service_requests_service_id_fkey'),
            ('service_requests_form_version_id_fkey',       'work_item_service_requests_form_version_id_fkey'),
            ('service_requests_requester_user_id_fkey',     'work_item_service_requests_requester_user_id_fkey'),
            ('service_requests_requested_for_user_id_fkey', 'work_item_service_requests_requested_for_user_id_fkey'),
            ('service_requests_assigned_group_id_fkey',     'work_item_service_requests_assigned_group_id_fkey'),
            ('service_requests_assigned_user_id_fkey',      'work_item_service_requests_assigned_user_id_fkey'),
            ('service_requests_created_by_fkey',            'work_item_service_requests_created_by_fkey'),
            ('service_requests_updated_by_fkey',            'work_item_service_requests_updated_by_fkey'),
            ('service_requests_id_not_null',                    'work_item_service_requests_id_not_null'),
            ('service_requests_request_number_not_null',        'work_item_service_requests_request_number_not_null'),
            ('service_requests_service_id_not_null',            'work_item_service_requests_service_id_not_null'),
            ('service_requests_form_version_id_not_null',       'work_item_service_requests_form_version_id_not_null'),
            ('service_requests_urgency_not_null',               'work_item_service_requests_urgency_not_null'),
            ('service_requests_status_not_null',                'work_item_service_requests_status_not_null'),
            ('service_requests_title_not_null',                 'work_item_service_requests_title_not_null'),
            ('service_requests_answers_not_null',               'work_item_service_requests_answers_not_null'),
            ('service_requests_requester_user_id_not_null',     'work_item_service_requests_requester_user_id_not_null'),
            ('service_requests_created_by_not_null',            'work_item_service_requests_created_by_not_null'),
            ('service_requests_created_at_not_null',            'work_item_service_requests_created_at_not_null'),
            ('service_requests_updated_at_not_null',            'work_item_service_requests_updated_at_not_null')
        ) AS t(old_name, new_name)
    LOOP
        IF EXISTS (
            SELECT 1
            FROM pg_constraint c
            JOIN pg_class rel ON rel.oid = c.conrelid
            JOIN pg_namespace n ON n.oid = rel.relnamespace
            WHERE n.nspname = 'app'
              AND rel.relname = 'work_item_service_requests'
              AND c.conname = rec.old_name
        ) THEN
            EXECUTE format(
                'ALTER TABLE app.work_item_service_requests RENAME CONSTRAINT %I TO %I',
                rec.old_name, rec.new_name
            );
        END IF;
    END LOOP;
END $$;

-- ===========================================================================
-- 10. Trigger functions (rename, then replace body so the sequence name matches)
-- ===========================================================================

DO $$
BEGIN
    IF to_regprocedure('app.tgr_service_requests_assign_number()') IS NOT NULL
       AND to_regprocedure('app.tgr_work_item_service_requests_assign_number()') IS NULL
    THEN
        ALTER FUNCTION app.tgr_service_requests_assign_number()
            RENAME TO tgr_work_item_service_requests_assign_number;
    END IF;

    IF to_regprocedure('app.tgr_service_requests_stamp_immutable()') IS NOT NULL
       AND to_regprocedure('app.tgr_work_item_service_requests_stamp_immutable()') IS NULL
    THEN
        ALTER FUNCTION app.tgr_service_requests_stamp_immutable()
            RENAME TO tgr_work_item_service_requests_stamp_immutable;
    END IF;
END $$;

CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION app.tgr_work_item_service_requests_assign_number()
RETURNS trigger
LANGUAGE plpgsql
AS $$
BEGIN
    IF NEW.request_number IS NOT NULL AND btrim(NEW.request_number) <> '' THEN
        RETURN NEW;
    END IF;

    NEW.request_number := app.work_item_id_prefix('service_request'::app.work_item_kind)
        || app.int_to_base36_6(nextval('app.seq_work_item_service_request_number'));
    RETURN NEW;
END;
$$;

CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION app.tgr_work_item_service_requests_stamp_immutable()
RETURNS trigger
LANGUAGE plpgsql
AS $$
DECLARE
    deleted_user CONSTANT UUID := '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000dead';
BEGIN
    IF NEW.request_number       IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.request_number
       OR NEW.service_id          IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.service_id
       OR NEW.form_version_id     IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.form_version_id
       OR NEW.created_at          IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.created_at
       OR (
            NEW.requester_user_id IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.requester_user_id
            AND NEW.requester_user_id IS DISTINCT FROM deleted_user
          )
    THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'service request %: submission stamp is immutable', OLD.id
            USING ERRCODE = '23514';
    END IF;
    RETURN NEW;
END;
$$;

-- ===========================================================================
-- 11. Triggers on the renamed table (shared tgr_set_updated_at is not renamed)
-- ===========================================================================

DO $$
DECLARE
    rec record;
BEGIN
    FOR rec IN
        SELECT * FROM (VALUES
            ('tgr_service_requests_set_updated_at',  'tgr_work_item_service_requests_set_updated_at'),
            ('tgr_service_requests_assign_number',   'tgr_work_item_service_requests_assign_number'),
            ('tgr_service_requests_stamp_immutable', 'tgr_work_item_service_requests_stamp_immutable')
        ) AS t(old_name, new_name)
    LOOP
        IF EXISTS (
            SELECT 1
            FROM pg_trigger trg
            JOIN pg_class rel ON rel.oid = trg.tgrelid
            JOIN pg_namespace n ON n.oid = rel.relnamespace
            WHERE n.nspname = 'app'
              AND rel.relname = 'work_item_service_requests'
              AND trg.tgname = rec.old_name
              AND NOT trg.tgisinternal
        ) THEN
            EXECUTE format(
                'ALTER TRIGGER %I ON app.work_item_service_requests RENAME TO %I',
                rec.old_name, rec.new_name
            );
        END IF;
    END LOOP;
END $$;

-- Fallback: create any of the three triggers if it is still missing under its
-- final name (e.g. a from-scratch apply of this single file with no prior
-- service_requests table at all — matches a fresh install taking db/init instead,
-- but keeps this file self-sufficient if ever run standalone).
DO $$
BEGIN
    IF NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM pg_trigger trg
        JOIN pg_class rel ON rel.oid = trg.tgrelid
        JOIN pg_namespace n ON n.oid = rel.relnamespace
        WHERE n.nspname = 'app'
          AND rel.relname = 'work_item_service_requests'
          AND trg.tgname = 'tgr_work_item_service_requests_set_updated_at'
          AND NOT trg.tgisinternal
    ) THEN
        CREATE TRIGGER tgr_work_item_service_requests_set_updated_at
        BEFORE UPDATE ON app.work_item_service_requests
        FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION app.tgr_set_updated_at();
    END IF;

    IF NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM pg_trigger trg
        JOIN pg_class rel ON rel.oid = trg.tgrelid
        JOIN pg_namespace n ON n.oid = rel.relnamespace
        WHERE n.nspname = 'app'
          AND rel.relname = 'work_item_service_requests'
          AND trg.tgname = 'tgr_work_item_service_requests_assign_number'
          AND NOT trg.tgisinternal
    ) THEN
        CREATE TRIGGER tgr_work_item_service_requests_assign_number
        BEFORE INSERT ON app.work_item_service_requests
        FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION app.tgr_work_item_service_requests_assign_number();
    END IF;

    IF NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM pg_trigger trg
        JOIN pg_class rel ON rel.oid = trg.tgrelid
        JOIN pg_namespace n ON n.oid = rel.relnamespace
        WHERE n.nspname = 'app'
          AND rel.relname = 'work_item_service_requests'
          AND trg.tgname = 'tgr_work_item_service_requests_stamp_immutable'
          AND NOT trg.tgisinternal
    ) THEN
        CREATE TRIGGER tgr_work_item_service_requests_stamp_immutable
        BEFORE UPDATE ON app.work_item_service_requests
        FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION app.tgr_work_item_service_requests_stamp_immutable();
    END IF;
END $$;

-- ===========================================================================
-- 12. COMMENT ON — same literals as db/init (dump-visible parity)
-- ===========================================================================

COMMENT ON TABLE app.work_item_service_requests IS
    'Submitted service requests. Each row stamps catalog origin (service, frozen form version) and stores title, description, answers, urgency, impact, priority, status, pause_reason, channel, quantity, work_notes, watch_list, assignment pointers, and resolved/closed timestamps. channel is always NULL until inbound channels exist. impact, priority, watch_list, quantity, work_notes, pause_reason, assignment and resolved/closed stamps are stored only — no fill logic in this release.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.request_number IS 'Human-readable reference sr- + 6 base36 chars from app.seq_work_item_service_request_number; assigned by trigger on INSERT. Unique. Immutable after INSERT.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.title IS 'Short title of the request. Promoted so lists and search need no JSONB walk. Required and non-blank.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.description IS 'Free-text description stored as its own column, not inside answers. Nullable; no fill logic in this release — set manually.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.impact IS 'Impact level (low/medium/high/critical). Stored only; no fill logic and no priority calculation from impact and urgency in this release.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.priority IS 'Priority level (low/medium/high/critical). Stored only; set manually. This release does not compute priority from impact and urgency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.watch_list IS 'Array of watcher user ids. Nullable; no FK and no fill logic in this release.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.quantity IS 'Quantity for product orders. Nullable; no fill logic in this release — set manually.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.work_notes IS 'Internal support notes, not visible to the requester. Nullable; no fill logic in this release — set manually.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.channel IS 'How the request reached the system (app.work_item_channel). Nullable, no default; always NULL in this release until inbound channels exist. Not part of the immutable submission stamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.answers IS 'Filled form as {fieldKey: value} (camelCase keys mirror the form definition). Structure is validated by the application against the stamped form version, not by the DB.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.requester_user_id IS 'Who raised the request. ON DELETE SET DEFAULT → seeded Deleted User so hard-deleting the account does not require closing requests.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.requested_for_user_id IS 'Beneficiary when different from the requester; NULL means self. ON DELETE SET DEFAULT → Deleted User (preserves that a beneficiary existed).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.created_by IS 'Audit author of the row (same as requester at portal submit). ON DELETE SET DEFAULT → Deleted User.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.assigned_group_id IS 'Group currently responsible. Stored only; no fill logic and no read-access derivation from this column plus support tiers in this release.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.assigned_user_id IS 'User currently assigned. Nullable. Stored only; no fill logic in this release.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.pause_reason IS
    'Why the request is on hold. Stored only; no fill or clear-on-resume logic in this release, and no CHECK tying it to status. The four values separate waits by whose clock they are on: awaiting_requester and awaiting_third_party are outside the support team''s control, scheduled is planned work, other is everything else.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.resolved_at IS 'Resolution timestamp. Stored only; no fill logic and no CHECK tying it to status in this release.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.closed_at IS 'Closed timestamp. Stored only; no fill logic and no CHECK tying it to status in this release.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.status IS
    'Work-item lifecycle status (app.work_item_status). Approval outcomes live on approval_status, not here. Stored only; no fill logic and no CHECK tying resolved_at, closed_at or pause_reason to this column in this release.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.work_item_service_requests.approval_status IS
    'Approval outcome (app.work_item_approval_status), decoupled from status. Default not_required. Stored only; no fill or compute logic in this release.';

-- ===========================================================================
-- 13. KB content versioning (generic content_version/content_hash)
-- ===========================================================================

ALTER TABLE app.kb_trees ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS content_version BIGINT NOT NULL DEFAULT 1;
ALTER TABLE app.kb_trees ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS content_hash VARCHAR(80);
ALTER TABLE app.kb_nodes ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS content_version BIGINT NOT NULL DEFAULT 1;
ALTER TABLE app.kb_nodes ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS content_hash VARCHAR(80);
ALTER TABLE app.kb_articles ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS content_version BIGINT NOT NULL DEFAULT 1;
ALTER TABLE app.kb_articles ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS content_hash VARCHAR(80);

COMMENT ON COLUMN app.kb_trees.content_version IS 'Monotonic per-entity content revision counter, bumped whenever this row''s canonical content (translations + significant metadata) changes. Independent of system_content_version (whole-template semver, system trees only). Applies to every tree, user-authored or system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.kb_trees.content_hash IS 'sha256 hex digest of this row''s canonical content, used to detect whether content_version must bump. Nullable: lazily computed on first edit for pre-existing rows — NULL means "not yet computed", not "no content".';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.kb_nodes.content_version IS 'Monotonic per-entity content revision counter, bumped whenever this row''s canonical content (translations + significant metadata) changes. Independent of system_content_version (whole-template semver, system trees only). Applies to every tree, user-authored or system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.kb_nodes.content_hash IS 'sha256 hex digest of this row''s canonical content, used to detect whether content_version must bump. Nullable: lazily computed on first edit for pre-existing rows — NULL means "not yet computed", not "no content".';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.kb_articles.content_version IS 'Monotonic per-entity content revision counter, bumped whenever this row''s canonical content (translations + significant metadata) changes. Independent of system_content_version (whole-template semver, system trees only). Applies to every tree, user-authored or system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN app.kb_articles.content_hash IS 'sha256 hex digest of this row''s canonical content, used to detect whether content_version must bump. Nullable: lazily computed on first edit for pre-existing rows — NULL means "not yet computed", not "no content".';

